00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:25.350
I know I did that when I
was a kid with my friends.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.748
Like I would speak like them
and move like them sometimes

00:06:27.748 --> 00:06:28.581
without even knowing.

00:06:28.581 --> 00:06:31.278
So I consciously took her
on 'cause it's my job.

00:06:31.278 --> 00:06:32.969
And it was so fun.

00:06:32.969 --> 00:06:33.802
- That's so cool.

00:06:33.802 --> 00:06:34.919
- I know nothing about her.

00:06:34.919 --> 00:06:37.111
- What a cool job though.
I love that. I love it.

00:06:37.111 --> 00:06:38.642
So wait, what was the
trick to figuring out?

00:06:38.642 --> 00:06:40.390
Because her voice was pretty deep.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:41.347
It was different than yours.

00:06:41.347 --> 00:06:42.199
- Yeah. Very different.

00:06:42.199 --> 00:06:44.236
I mean, as a singer, I like-

00:06:44.236 --> 00:06:46.378
- Like I'm a soprano, it's hard
for me to go low like that.

00:06:46.378 --> 00:06:48.690
- Well, so I think we naturally sit

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:50.442
at an above average levels.

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:51.275
There's like a measurement.

00:06:51.275 --> 00:06:52.536
- It's like higher the
frequency of... Yeah, yeah.

00:06:52.536 --> 00:06:56.949
- Yeah. And she, at her deepest
spoke, just insanely low,

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:57.782
and it's impo...

00:06:57.782 --> 00:07:00.551
It's physically impossible
for us to speak that low.

00:07:00.551 --> 00:07:02.382
But, you know, I have a version of it.

00:07:02.382 --> 00:07:05.670
My lowest is what I used
and I try to protect myself

00:07:05.670 --> 00:07:06.590
with my voice coach.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.053
Like she really helped me
try to protect my voice,

00:07:09.053 --> 00:07:11.422
