and see what's changed and
support it and whatever.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.156
And I did and they were awesome.

00:08:40.156 --> 00:08:42.594
I went to my husband's a theater guy

00:08:42.594 --> 00:08:44.462
and I was never in the
theater department in school.

00:08:44.462 --> 00:08:46.416
I did not act in school
'cause I was intermediate.

00:08:46.416 --> 00:08:47.434
- That's ironic.

00:08:47.434 --> 00:08:48.886
- I know it's weird. It was weird.

00:08:48.886 --> 00:08:49.916
I was only singing though.

00:08:49.916 --> 00:08:52.390
And I went and I saw
this guy, Mr. Sackler,

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:55.806
who's like local famous theater director.

00:08:55.806 --> 00:08:57.200
And he was talking to me.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.390
He was like showing us the black box

00:08:58.390 --> 00:08:59.500
and showing us all these cool things.

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:00.864
He's like, "This is the
show we're doing next."

00:09:00.864 --> 00:09:01.697
And my husband's like,

00:09:01.697 --> 00:09:02.868
"Wow, what a cool school you went to?"

00:09:02.868 --> 00:09:04.940
And I was like, "I was never
a part of any of this."

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:05.804
And he had no idea.

00:09:05.804 --> 00:09:08.241
And he mentioned me and I had my mask on.

00:09:08.241 --> 00:09:09.074
- Wait, the teacher?

00:09:09.074 --> 00:09:10.202
- The teacher mentioned me.

00:09:10.202 --> 00:09:12.042
He's like, (indistinct)

00:09:12.042 --> 00:09:14.072
And I pulled my mask down and I was like,

00:09:14.072 --> 00:09:15.420
"I should probably...

00:09:15.420 --> 00:09:18.304
I feel like I'm lying to you."

00:09:18.304 --> 00:09:20.623
And I took my mask down and he screamed

00:09:20.623 --> 00:09:21.487
and ran across the room.

00:09:21.487 --> 00:09:24.117
And it was like the most
amazing thing I'd ever seen.

00:09:24.117 --> 00:09:25.774
Most amazing like reaction.

00:09:25.774 --> 00:09:26.607
And I realized that like-

00:09:26.607 --> 00:09:27.765
- Oh, I love that he didn't know.

00:09:27.765 --> 00:09:29.718
- Yeah. And it was amazing for him.

00:09:29.718 --> 00:09:30.903
And I was like, "I'll come back

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.293
and talk to your theater students."

00:09:32.293 --> 00:09:33.126
'Cause like-

00:09:33.126 --> 00:09:33.959
- Even if you have a mask on,

00:09:33.959 --> 00:09:35.621
you have like the most recognizable eyes

00:09:35.621 --> 00:09:36.921
on all of the lands.

00:09:36.921 --> 00:09:38.844
- I think he's just
super busy in his head.

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:41.603
- Okay. I was like, he is not observant.

00:09:41.603 --> 00:09:43.290
- No. And I think he knows that.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.304
And it was so cute.

00:09:45.304 --> 00:09:47.312
He was like, ah!

00:09:47.312 --> 00:09:48.414
I was like, "Oh my God, thank you."

00:09:48.414 --> 00:09:49.445
- Oh, I love that.

00:09:49.445 --> 00:09:51.282
- And so he lives with us now

00:09:51.282 --> 00:09:53.747
because it was very
flattering (indistinct)

00:09:53.747 --> 00:09:54.862
- He lives with us now.

00:09:54.862 --> 00:09:56.150
- No, but it was at school.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:58.082
Go back to high school if you can.

00:09:58.082 --> 00:10:01.867
If you were traumatized in
high school, try to go back.

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:02.868
It might help.

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:04.614
- What was traumatizing?
I wasn't traumatized.

00:10:04.614 --> 00:10:06.962
I just didn't wanna be there.

00:10:06.962 --> 00:10:09.619
- I didn't wanna be
there. It was girl stuff.

00:10:09.619 --> 00:10:10.642
- Oh, girls are mean.

00:10:10.642 --> 00:10:12.095
See, that's why...

00:10:12.095 --> 00:10:14.486
I had a few like good,
solid, like girlfriends. Yeah

00:10:14.486 --> 00:10:16.374
- I did too. I'm still best
friends with my girlfriend.

00:10:16.374 --> 00:10:17.573
We have a company together.

00:10:17.573 --> 00:10:18.792
Like we really talk every day.

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:20.418
- No people are mean, girls
are mean, I will say that.

00:10:20.418 --> 00:10:22.052
Girls are really mean. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:22.052 --> 00:10:23.903
- And now if I run into
them in town, we'll be like,

00:10:23.903 --> 00:10:25.364
"Oh, Hey, how are you doing?"

00:10:25.364 --> 00:10:27.229
But like in high school, it was like-

00:10:27.229 --> 00:10:28.331
- I know, but here's the best part, girl.

00:10:28.331 --> 00:10:29.449
You don't even need to run into them.

00:10:29.449 --> 00:10:30.774
They could just watch you.

00:10:30.774 --> 00:10:31.607
Hey!

00:10:31.607 --> 00:10:32.572
(Audience applauding)

00:10:32.572 --> 00:10:35.061
Oh, but you are about
to go to college though

00:10:35.061 --> 00:10:36.820
when Mean Girls happened, right?

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:37.972
Like you were at college, right?

00:10:37.972 --> 00:10:39.790
You were going to college and then-

00:10:39.790 --> 00:10:42.063
- I was enrolled in Fordham. Yeah.

00:10:42.063 --> 00:10:44.968
- Oh my gosh. Was that a
hard decision to like..

00:10:44.968 --> 00:10:47.092
"Cause nobody knew what it was gonna be.

00:10:47.092 --> 00:10:48.703
- Nobody knew. No, no.

00:10:48.703 --> 00:10:50.753
I will tell you, it
wasn't a decision I made.

00:10:50.753 --> 00:10:51.859
I did not make that decision.

00:10:51.859 --> 00:10:52.850
- Wait, who made it?

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:55.898
- Mark Waters who directed
Mean Girls made the decision

00:10:55.898 --> 00:10:57.360
to cast me as Karen.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:59.548
And I was like, "Oh, I guess,
I can even go to college."

00:10:59.548 --> 00:11:01.924
I mean, I missed my first
class anyway 'cause I was late

00:11:01.924 --> 00:11:02.950
because of the audition.

00:11:02.950 --> 00:11:03.800
It was all fate.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:06.918
Guys, the universe was screaming at me

00:11:06.918 --> 00:11:10.177
that I did not belong
in a college setting.

00:11:10.177 --> 00:11:12.052
And I appreciate that.

00:11:12.052 --> 00:11:12.885
- Thank you universe.

00:11:12.885 --> 00:11:15.607
- The luck of getting
Mean Girls, like what?

00:11:15.607 --> 00:11:17.484
- Well, and the luck, you got
it though for a good reason.

00:11:17.484 --> 00:11:18.692
You were amazing.

00:11:18.692 --> 00:11:21.225
It's such a funny just movie
to watch for all of us.

00:11:21.225 --> 00:11:22.058
So we related to..

00:11:22.058 --> 00:11:24.205
It's so relatable, such a
big huge pop culture moment.

00:11:24.205 --> 00:11:25.521
And it was like 18 years ago, right?

00:11:25.521 --> 00:11:26.354
- It was 18 years ago.
- It was 18 years.

00:11:26.354 --> 00:11:27.821
Do you still talk to all them?

00:11:27.821 --> 00:11:29.184
- Yeah, I do.
- That's cool.

00:11:29.184 --> 00:11:31.361
- Yeah. I mean, especially Lacey.

00:11:31.361 --> 00:11:33.865
- She's been here a few
times. She's lovely.

00:11:33.865 --> 00:11:35.902
- She is who she... Like just like you.

00:11:35.902 --> 00:11:37.277
- She's so nice.

00:11:37.277 --> 00:11:38.341
- The same as she present.

00:11:38.341 --> 00:11:40.728
- Like on and off? Oh that's nice.

00:11:40.728 --> 00:11:42.255
Yeah. I know you look like a little baby.

00:11:42.255 --> 00:11:43.299
- We had the best time.

00:11:43.299 --> 00:11:44.279
- Yeah. I love that.

00:11:44.279 --> 00:11:45.955
- It was the best.
- I love that you have...

00:11:45.955 --> 00:11:47.936
That was your first like
big experience, right?

00:11:47.936 --> 00:11:50.036
In the industry? That's awesome.

00:11:50.036 --> 00:11:50.960
- Listen, I'm still...

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:52.868
I think I'm just not jaded.

00:11:52.868 --> 00:11:54.247
I think I'm just like-
- That's amazing.

00:11:54.247 --> 00:11:55.413
- That was the best thing.

00:11:55.413 --> 00:11:56.355
- Stay there. Yeah.

00:11:56.355 --> 00:11:57.188
- I mean, I'll try.

